
§§ `Hand-written cases: exact words of a charge`

-- s 311, infanticide
-- @fixture `Infanticide by a mother after birth` OF `Infanticide Facts`
-- S victim = "Baby Lim"
-- S the manner = "by smothering the said child"
-- T the accused is a woman
-- T by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child
-- T the child is below 12 months of age
-- T the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s section EQUALS "311"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s offence EQUALS "infanticide"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if she is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did, being a woman, by an intentional act or omission cause the death of her child, one Baby Lim, a child below 12 months of age, at a time when the balance of your mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of giving birth to the said child or of lactation, and thereby commit the offence of infanticide, to wit, by smothering the said child, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 311 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 310: the child is below 12 months; at 12 months it is not (the helper's line)
#ASSERT `below 12 months of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT (`below 12 months of age` 12)
-- s 310 does not make "murder but for this section" an element ("notwithstanding that ..."): the ladder asks only for the woman, the act, the child and the disturbance
-- s 304C(4), by the accused's own act
-- @fixture `Household death by A's own act` OF `Household Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by striking the said child repeatedly"
-- T B is below 14 years of age
-- T B dies as a result of an unlawful act
-- T the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B
-- T the person who did that act had frequent contact with B
-- T A was a member of the same household as B
-- T A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act
-- T at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person
-- T A was the person whose act caused B's death
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's own act`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's own act`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a member of the same household as one Lim Mei Ling and having frequent contact with the said person, did by your own unlawful act cause the death of the said person, to wit, by striking the said child repeatedly, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304C(4) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 304C(4), by failing to protect (the second alternative of (1)(d))
-- @fixture `Household death by A's failure to protect` OF `Household Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by failing to protect the said child from repeated assaults by another member of the household"
-- T B is below 14 years of age
-- T B dies as a result of an unlawful act
-- T the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B
-- T the person who did that act had frequent contact with B
-- T A was a member of the same household as B
-- T A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act
-- T at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person
-- T A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk
-- T A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk
-- T the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's failure to protect`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's failure to protect`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a member of the same household as one Lim Mei Ling and having frequent contact with the said person, did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take to protect the said person from a significant risk of grievous hurt, whereby the said person died as a result of the unlawful act of a member of the same household, to wit, by failing to protect the said child from repeated assaults by another member of the household, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304C(4) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 304C(3): "A is not guilty of an offence under this section if A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step"
-- (the first alternative is by A's own act: step-taking is not in question there; the flat negative reading applies to the whole offence: FORK DEF-A4)
-- @fixture `Household death, failure to protect, A could not have been expected to act` OF `Household Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by failing to protect the said child"
-- T B is below 14 years of age
-- T B dies as a result of an unlawful act
-- T the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B
-- T the person who did that act had frequent contact with B
-- T A was a member of the same household as B
-- T A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act
-- T at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person
-- T A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk
-- T A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk
-- T the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen
-- T A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death, failure to protect, A could not have been expected to act`)
#ASSERT NOT (`charge under s 304C(4)` `Household death, failure to protect, A could not have been expected to act`)'s `made out`
-- s 304C(2): the prosecution need not prove which alternative of (1)(d) applies: both together make the offence out too
-- @fixture `Household death, both alternatives of (1)(d)` OF `Household Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by the act charged"
-- T B is below 14 years of age
-- T B dies as a result of an unlawful act
-- T the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B
-- T the person who did that act had frequent contact with B
-- T A was a member of the same household as B
-- T A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act
-- T at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person
-- T A was the person whose act caused B's death
-- T A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk
-- T A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk
-- T the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death, both alternatives of (1)(d)`
-- s 308A(2), with the Illustration
-- Illustration: three members of a group including A decide to rob a neighbourhood shop. The group leader B brings a sharp knife but reassures A that the knife is only
-- to be used to threaten the shopkeeper C. A believes B and takes part. B then stabs C, who dies. "A is guilty of an offence under this section because A knew that the
-- knife was to be used to threaten another person, C, in furtherance of the group's common object to commit robbery."
-- A did not know that death or grievous hurt was likely; A knew a deadly weapon was to be used against another person.
-- @fixture `Group object death, the knife Illustration` OF `Group Object Death Facts`
-- S victim = "C"
-- S the manner = "B stabbed the said C with a knife in the course of a robbery"
-- T the accused is or acts as a member of a group
-- T the accused knows that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law
-- T the accused knows that a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner against another person in the furtherance of that common object
-- T the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 308A(2)` `Group object death, the knife Illustration`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 308A(2)` `Group object death, the knife Illustration`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 308A(2)` `Group object death, the knife Illustration`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to caning"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 308A(2)` `Group object death, the knife Illustration`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being or acting as a member of a group, knowing that the common object of the members of the group was to commit an offence, and knowing that a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, was to be used against another person in the furtherance of that common object, did, the death of one C having been caused in furtherance of that common object, to wit, B stabbed the said C with a knife in the course of a robbery, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 308A(2) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- the other limb of (b): knowledge that death or grievous hurt is likely
-- @fixture `Group object death, death likely` OF `Group Object Death Facts`
-- S victim = "C"
-- S the manner = "B stabbed the said C"
-- T the accused is or acts as a member of a group
-- T the accused knows that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law
-- T the accused knows that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object
-- T the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object
-- @end
#ASSERT (`charge under s 308A(2)` `Group object death, death likely`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being or acting as a member of a group, knowing that the common object of the members of the group was to commit an offence, and knowing that death or grievous hurt was likely to be caused in furtherance of that common object, did, the death of one C having been caused in furtherance of that common object, to wit, B stabbed the said C, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 308A(2) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 314: the Explanation, "It is not essential to this offence that the offender should know that the act is likely to cause death": the answer changes nothing
-- @fixture `Miscarriage death, offender knows` OF `Miscarriage Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by administering a noxious drug"
-- T not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974
-- T the woman is with child
-- T the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman
-- T the act causes the death of the woman
-- T the offender knows that the act is likely to cause death
-- @end
-- @fixture `Miscarriage death, offender does not know` OF `Miscarriage Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by administering a noxious drug"
-- T not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974
-- T the woman is with child
-- T the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman
-- T the act causes the death of the woman
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 314` `Miscarriage death, offender knows`
#ASSERT `offence under s 314` `Miscarriage death, offender does not know`
-- knowledge alone, with nothing else, is not the offence
-- @fixture `Miscarriage death, knowledge alone` OF `Miscarriage Death Facts`
-- T the offender knows that the act is likely to cause death
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 314` `Miscarriage death, knowledge alone`)
-- the punishment follows the woman's consent: with consent, the 10 years and fine; without, life or the above
#ASSERT (`charge under s 314` `Miscarriage death, offender does not know`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
-- @fixture `Miscarriage death, without her consent` OF `Miscarriage Death Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by administering a noxious drug"
-- T not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974
-- T the woman is with child
-- T the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman
-- T the act causes the death of the woman
-- T the act is done without the consent of the woman
-- @end
#ASSERT (`charge under s 314` `Miscarriage death, without her consent`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for life, or with the punishment above-mentioned"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 314` `Miscarriage death, without her consent`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, with intent to cause the miscarriage of one Lim Mei Ling, a woman with child, did an act which caused her death, the act being done without her consent, to wit, by administering a noxious drug, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 314 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 314` `Miscarriage death, offender does not know`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, with intent to cause the miscarriage of one Lim Mei Ling, a woman with child, did an act which caused her death, to wit, by administering a noxious drug, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 314 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 315(1), before or after birth
-- @fixture `Child destruction before birth` OF `Child Destruction Facts`
-- S victim = "a female child capable of being born alive"
-- S the manner = "by compressing the head of the child"
-- T not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974
-- T the accused intends to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive
-- T by an intentional act causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother
-- @end
#ASSERT (`charge under s 315(1)` `Child destruction before birth`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive, did by an intentional act cause one a female child capable of being born alive to die before it had an existence independent of its mother, to wit, by compressing the head of the child, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 315(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 315(1) "unless such act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother"
-- @fixture `Child destruction to save the mother` OF `Child Destruction Facts`
-- T not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974
-- T the accused intends to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive
-- T by an intentional act causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother
-- T the act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 315(1)` `Child destruction to save the mother`)

§§ `ss 304B and 304C - definitions and rules of reading`

-- s 304B(2) "child" means a person below 14 years of age: the text says no to anyone of 14 or over
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the person is a child` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the person is a child` 13 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the person is a child` 14 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the person is a child` 40 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 304B(2) "sustained abuse": (a) 2 or more occasions
#ASSERT NOT (`2 or more occasions` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`2 or more occasions` 1)
#ASSERT `2 or more occasions` 2
#ASSERT `2 or more occasions` 3
-- s 304B(2) "neglect" means the failure to provide any or adequate essential care to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain, or injury to the physical health
-- @fixture `Neglect, failure and injury` OF `Neglect Facts`
-- T fails to provide any or adequate essential care
-- T to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain, or injury to physical health
-- @end
-- @fixture `Neglect, failure only` OF `Neglect Facts`
-- T fails to provide any or adequate essential care
-- @end
-- @fixture `Neglect, injury only` OF `Neglect Facts`
-- T to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain, or injury to physical health
-- @end
-- @fixture `Neglect, nothing` OF `Neglect Facts`
-- @end
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the failure is neglect` `Neglect, failure and injury` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the failure is neglect` `Neglect, failure only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the failure is neglect` `Neglect, injury only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 304B(2) the failure is neglect` `Neglect, nothing` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 304B(2) "relevant person": (a) a child's custodian; (b) a domestic worker's employer, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent; (c) a vulnerable person's custodian
-- the same person is not a relevant person in respect of another kind of victim
-- @fixture `Abuse, custodian of a child` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the victim is a child below 14 years of age
-- T the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, custodian of a domestic worker` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the victim is a domestic worker
-- T the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, employer of a domestic worker` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the victim is a domestic worker
-- T the accused is the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, custodian of a vulnerable person` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the victim is a vulnerable person
-- T the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, employer of a child` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the victim is a child below 14 years of age
-- T the accused is the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker
-- @end
#ASSERT `relevant person within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, custodian of a child`
#ASSERT NOT (`relevant person within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, custodian of a domestic worker`)
#ASSERT `relevant person within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, employer of a domestic worker`
#ASSERT `relevant person within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, custodian of a vulnerable person`
#ASSERT NOT (`relevant person within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, employer of a child`)
-- s 304B(2) "sustained abuse": hurt or neglect, on 2 or more occasions or once if protracted
-- @fixture `Abuse, hurt on two occasions` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the conduct consists of voluntarily causing hurt
-- T the conduct took place on 2 or more occasions
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, neglect once and protracted` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the conduct consists of knowingly causing neglect
-- T the conduct took place on a single occasion and was protracted
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, hurt once and not protracted` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the conduct consists of voluntarily causing hurt
-- @end
-- @fixture `Abuse, occasions without hurt or neglect` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- T the conduct took place on 2 or more occasions
-- @end
#ASSERT `sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, hurt on two occasions`
#ASSERT `sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, neglect once and protracted`
#ASSERT NOT (`sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, hurt once and not protracted`)
#ASSERT NOT (`sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` `Abuse, occasions without hurt or neglect`)
-- s 304B(1), the three kinds of victim in the charge
-- @fixture `Sustained abuse killing a domestic worker` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by repeatedly striking the said domestic worker and withholding food"
-- T the victim is a domestic worker
-- T the accused is the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker
-- T the conduct consists of voluntarily causing hurt
-- T the conduct took place on 2 or more occasions
-- T causes the death of the victim by the course of conduct
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 304B(1)` `Sustained abuse killing a domestic worker`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304B(1)` `Sustained abuse killing a domestic worker`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a relevant person, did cause the death of one Lim Mei Ling, a domestic worker, by sustained abuse, to wit, by repeatedly striking the said domestic worker and withholding food, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304B(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304B(1)` `Sustained abuse killing a domestic worker`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for life and shall also be liable to caning; or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 30 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
-- @fixture `Sustained abuse killing a vulnerable person` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by leaving the said person without food"
-- T the victim is a vulnerable person
-- T the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim
-- T the conduct consists of knowingly causing neglect
-- T the conduct took place on a single occasion and was protracted
-- T causes the death of the victim by the course of conduct
-- @end
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304B(1)` `Sustained abuse killing a vulnerable person`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a relevant person, did cause the death of one Lim Mei Ling, a vulnerable person, by sustained abuse, to wit, by leaving the said person without food, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304B(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- @fixture `Sustained abuse killing a child` OF `Sustained Abuse Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by repeatedly striking the said child"
-- T the victim is a child below 14 years of age
-- T the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim
-- T the conduct consists of voluntarily causing hurt
-- T the conduct took place on 2 or more occasions
-- T causes the death of the victim by the course of conduct
-- @end
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304B(1)` `Sustained abuse killing a child`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a relevant person, did cause the death of one Lim Mei Ling, a child below 14 years of age, by sustained abuse, to wit, by repeatedly striking the said child, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304B(1) of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 304C(5)(c) and s 335A(3): an "unlawful" act, other than an act by A, is one that constitutes an offence or would but for the actor's age, immaturity, unsoundness of mind, intoxication or mistake of fact
-- @fixture `Unlawful, an offence` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act constitutes an offence
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, by a child below the age in section 82` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person below the age specified in section 82
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, by a person of the age in section 83 without sufficient maturity` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of the act
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, by a person of unsound mind` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, by an intoxicated person` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, by a person who made a mistake of fact` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, an act of A` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- T the act is an act of A
-- T the act constitutes an offence
-- @end
-- @fixture `Unlawful, none of these` OF `Unlawful Act Facts`
-- @end
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a child below the age in section 82` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of the age in section 83 without sufficient maturity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of unsound mind` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by an intoxicated person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person who made a mistake of fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an act by A himself is outside the definition ("other than an act by A"): the text does not say what makes it unlawful (NOTHING-kind)
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an act of A` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an act that is none of these: the definition says "is one that ...", read as closed (marginal reading a)
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 335A(3): the same shape
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a child below the age in section 82` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of the age in section 83 without sufficient maturity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of unsound mind` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by an intoxicated person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person who made a mistake of fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an act of A` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 304C(5)(a): a person who does not live in the household is regarded as a member "if that person visits it so often and for such periods of time that it is reasonable"
-- a rule that adds members, so a person who does not meet it is not said to be a non-member (NOTHING-kind)
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(a) the person who does not live in the household is a member of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(a) the person who does not live in the household is a member of it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 304C(5)(b): where B lived in different households at different times, "the same household as B" is the one in which B was living at the time of the act
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(b) the household is the same household as B` "the household at 12 Jalan Besar" "the household at 12 Jalan Besar" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(b) the household is the same household as B` "the household at 12 Jalan Besar" "the household at 7 Bedok Road" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 304C(5)(e) and s 335A(4): A's circumstances "include but is not limited to" those experiences
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(e) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(e) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 335A(4) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(4) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 335A(6): "sexual abuse" means abuse caused to a victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010: a "means" definition
#ASSERT `s 335A(6) the abuse is sexual abuse` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(6) the abuse is sexual abuse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 315(2) - the length of a pregnancy`

-- "evidence that a woman had at any material time been pregnant for a period of 28 weeks or more shall be prima facie evidence that she was at that time pregnant of a child capable of being born alive"
#ASSERT NOT (`28 weeks or more` 27)
#ASSERT `28 weeks or more` 28
#ASSERT `28 weeks or more` 40
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 28 EQUALS `prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive`
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 36 EQUALS `prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive`
-- a shorter pregnancy: the subsection says nothing (a presumption limited by its own wording: NOTHING-kind, not "the child was not capable of being born alive")
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 27 EQUALS `not covered by s 315(2)`
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 0 EQUALS `not covered by s 315(2)`

§§ `s 316 - the hypothetical act, and the Illustration`

-- the hypothetical leaf is set from `commits culpable homicide` on the facts of the same act with the death caused (the module's comment says so)
-- Illustration: "A, knowing that he is likely to cause the death of a pregnant woman, does an act which, if it caused the death of the woman, would amount to culpable homicide.
-- The woman is injured, but does not die; but the death of an unborn quick child with which she is pregnant is thereby caused. A is guilty of the offence defined in this section."
-- @fixture `A would be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "the woman"
-- S the manner = "by striking the said woman in the abdomen with an iron bar"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death
-- @end
-- @fixture `no private defence` OF `Private Defence Facts`
-- @end
-- @fixture `A would not be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "the woman"
-- S the manner = "by the act charged"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- @end
#ASSERT `commits culpable homicide` `A would be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died`
#ASSERT NOT (`commits culpable homicide` `A would not be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died`)
-- @fixture `Quick unborn child killed by an act that would be culpable homicide` OF `Quick Unborn Child Facts`
-- E the accused does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide = `commits culpable homicide` `A would be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died`
-- S victim = "the quick unborn child of the said woman"
-- S the manner = "by striking the said woman in the abdomen with an iron bar"
-- T the accused by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 316` `Quick unborn child killed by an act that would be culpable homicide`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 316` `Quick unborn child killed by an act that would be culpable homicide`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 316` `Quick unborn child killed by an act that would be culpable homicide`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did an act under such circumstances that if you had thereby caused death you would have been guilty of culpable homicide, and did by such act cause the death of one the quick unborn child of the said woman, a quick unborn child, to wit, by striking the said woman in the abdomen with an iron bar, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 316 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- the act would not have been culpable homicide had the woman died: s 316 is not made out
-- @fixture `Quick unborn child killed by an act that would not be culpable homicide` OF `Quick Unborn Child Facts`
-- E the accused does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide = `commits culpable homicide` `A would not be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died`
-- S victim = "the quick unborn child of the said woman"
-- S the manner = "by the act charged"
-- T the accused by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 316` `Quick unborn child killed by an act that would not be culpable homicide`)

§§ `s 301(1) - the description of a transferred culpable homicide`

-- Z's death is intended; Y's death is caused. The facts "intended" are stated as if the accused had caused Z's death.
-- (a) intending to cause death: murder under s 300(a)
-- @fixture `Intended Z's death, the intention of causing death` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by shooting at Z"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the intention of causing death
-- @end
#ASSERT `commits murder` `Intended Z's death, the intention of causing death`
#ASSERT `s 301(1) the description of the culpable homicide` `Intended Z's death, the intention of causing death` TRUE EQUALS JUST `of the description of murder`
-- (b) knowing that death is likely, but not within s 300(a)-(d): culpable homicide not amounting to murder
-- @fixture `Intended Z's death, only knowledge that death was likely` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by throwing a brick at Z"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`commits murder` `Intended Z's death, only knowledge that death was likely`)
#ASSERT `commits culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `Intended Z's death, only knowledge that death was likely`
#ASSERT `s 301(1) the description of the culpable homicide` `Intended Z's death, only knowledge that death was likely` TRUE EQUALS JUST `of the description of culpable homicide not amounting to murder`
-- the intended killing would have fallen within Exception 1 (grave and sudden provocation by Z): the description is that of culpable homicide not amounting to murder
-- @fixture `Intended Z's death, provoked by Z` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by striking at Z, who had gravely and suddenly provoked the accused"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the intention of causing death
-- T whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation
-- T causes the death of the person who gave the provocation, or of any other person by mistake or accident
-- T the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person
-- T the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers
-- T the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`commits murder` `Intended Z's death, provoked by Z`)
#ASSERT `s 301(1) the description of the culpable homicide` `Intended Z's death, provoked by Z` TRUE EQUALS JUST `of the description of culpable homicide not amounting to murder`
-- the circumstances of s 301(1) are not these (no one else's death is caused): the section does not speak
#ASSERT `s 301(1) the description of the culpable homicide` `Intended Z's death, the intention of causing death` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the facts "as if Z had died" are not culpable homicide at all: the section names no description
-- @fixture `Intended Z's death, no culpable homicide` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by an accident"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`commits culpable homicide` `Intended Z's death, no culpable homicide`)
#ASSERT `s 301(1) the description of the culpable homicide` `Intended Z's death, no culpable homicide` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 335A - allowing neglect, hurt or abuse`

-- s 335A(5): death is not an element, it chooses the punishment (a) where death is caused, 7 years or fine up to $20,000 or both; (b) in any other case, 4 years or fine up to $4,000 or both
-- @fixture `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death` OF `Allowing Neglect Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by failing to report that the employer's son was repeatedly striking the said domestic worker"
-- T B is a domestic worker
-- T B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)
-- T A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C
-- T A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B
-- T A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk
-- T the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine which may extend to $4,000, or with both"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being the employer of one Lim Mei Ling, a domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or an employment agent of the said domestic worker, knowing or having reason to believe that the said domestic worker was at risk of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health caused by another person, did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take in your circumstances to protect the said domestic worker from that risk, whereby the said domestic worker suffered such harm as a result of the unlawful act of that person, in circumstances of the kind that you foresaw or ought to have foreseen, to wit, by failing to report that the employer's son was repeatedly striking the said domestic worker, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 335A(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- @fixture `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused` OF `Allowing Neglect Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by leaving the said person in the care of a known abuser"
-- T B is a vulnerable person
-- T B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)
-- T A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C
-- T A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B
-- T A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk
-- T the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen
-- T death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable person
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 335A(2)` `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 335A(2)` `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $20,000, or with both"
-- the two subsections are different offences: (1) needs a domestic worker and (2) a vulnerable person
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 335A(2)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`)
